    "<div>\n        <div>\n          <span>PART C</span>\n          <h3>READING (2.6 pts)</h3>\n        </div>\n        <span>Điền từ &amp; Đọc hiểu</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Part C.I: Cloze test -->\n      <div>\n        <h4>\n          I. Read the following passage and put a word in the box in each of the numbered blanks (1 pt)\n        </h4>\n\n        <!-- Cloze Passage Card -->\n        <div>\n          The country and the city have advantages and <strong>(1) _______</strong>. People in the country have beautiful surroundings. They enjoy <strong>(2) _______</strong> and quietness, and can do their work at their own pace because no one is in a hurry. They live in larger, more comfortable houses, and their neighbors are more friendly, and really willing to help them when they need. Their life, however, can be boring and they may be isolated, which is a serious problem <strong>(3) _______</strong> they are ill or want to take children to school. The city has all the services that the country doesn't, but it also has a lot of disadvantages. Cities are often polluted. They not <strong>(4) _______</strong> have polluted air but also have noisy streets. Everyone is always in a hurry and this <strong>(5) _______</strong> that people have no time to get to know each and make friends.\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- 5 Cloze Questions -->\n        <div>\n          <!-- Blank 1 -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Blank 2 -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Blank 3 -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Blank 4 -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Blank 5 -->\n          \n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Part C.II: Reading Comprehension -->\n      <div>\n        <h4>\n          II. Read the following passage and do the tasks below (1.6 pts)\n        </h4>\n\n        <!-- Reading Passage Card -->\n        <div>\n          The thing I liked most when I was small was the change of seasons. Spring, summer, autumn and winter - I could see <u>them</u> all come and go and each one was completely different. Now in the city, you can buy summer flowers in winter and eat the same vegetables all the year round. Whereas, in the country, I could only eat things at certain times of the year, for example, strawberries in June and turnips in winter. I lived my childhood with the seasons. We also made most of our food and would never eat frozen or tinned food. Everything was fresh, so it must be better than the type of food I am taking now in the city. City people may think people in the country miss a lot of things about modern life. In fact, in my opinion they miss a lot more than people in the country, they miss real life.\n        </div>\n\n        <div>\n          <!-- Question 1: Open ended -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Question 2: Yes/No -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Question 3: How was everything -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Question 4: Reference MCQ -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Question 5: Fact detail MCQ -->\n          \n        </div>\n      </div>",
    "<div>\n        <div>\n          <span>PART D</span>\n          <h3>WRITING</h3>\n        </div>\n        <span>Sắp xếp từ &amp; Viết lại câu</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- D.I: Rearrange with clickable interactive boxes -->\n      <div>\n        <div>\n          <h4>\n            I. Rearrange the words or phrases to make meaningful sentences. (0.6 pt)\n          </h4>\n        </div>\n        <p>\n          💡 <strong>Hướng dẫn:</strong> Bấm vào các thẻ từ/cụm từ bên dưới theo đúng thứ tự để tạo câu hoàn chỉnh. Bấm vào từ trong khung trả lời để gỡ bỏ. Dấu câu cuối câu (\".\", \"?\") sẽ được hệ thống tự động gán chuẩn xác khi hoàn thành!\n        </p>\n\n        <div>\n          <!-- Rearrange 1: new / showing/ things. /her/ My friend / likes/of/ -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Rearrange 2: on/ They/post/ medial. /pictures/ often/social/ -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Rearrange 3: keen / watching/ Are/ on /cartoons/ TV?/ they/on/ -->\n          \n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- D.II: Sentence Transformation (0.8 pt) -->\n      <div>\n        <h4>\n          II. Complete the second sentence so that it means the same as the sentence before. (0.8 pt)\n        </h4>\n\n        <div>\n          <!-- Question 1 -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Question 2 -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Question 3 -->\n          \n\n          <!-- Question 4 -->\n          \n        </div>\n      </div>"
